title: Msiexec Spawning Cmd to Launch a Script File
status: experimental
description: Detects msiexec.exe spawning cmd.exe with a command line that starts a .cmd script. Observed in the EtherRAT intrusion where a malicious MSI masquerading as a Sysinternals tool launched a .cmd file in a minimized window, which then downloaded a portable Node.js runtime.
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/05/11/flash-alert-etherrat-and-tuktuk-c2-end-in-the-gentleman-ransomware/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/21
tags:
    - attack.execution
    - attack.t1059.003
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
    service: sysmon
detection:
    selection_parent:
        ParentImage|endswith: '\msiexec.exe'
    selection_img:
        Image|endswith: '\cmd.exe'
    selection_cli_start:
        CommandLine|contains: 'start'
    selection_cli_script:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '.cmd'
            - '.bat'
            - '.vbs'
            - '.js'
            - '.ps1'
    condition: all of selection_*
    EventID: 1
fields:
    - ParentImage
    - Image
    - CommandLine
    - User
falsepositives:
    - Administrators or users legitimately installing software downloaded to these folders
level: low
